CAT = "aesiraEmergency"; SEG = "EMG"
Q = [
("Which number calls Dubai Police in an emergency?",
 "999", ["997", "998", "901"],
 "999 is the UAE police emergency number. 998 is the ambulance, 997 Civil Defence (fire) and 901 the Dubai Police non-emergency line."),
("A guard has called 998 for a visitor who collapsed in a tower lobby. How can the guard help the ambulance crew?",
 "Send someone to meet and guide them", ["Lock the lobby doors to keep calm", "Move the visitor to the car park", "Call 998 again every minute"],
 "998 is the UAE ambulance number. A person waiting at the entrance with a lift held ready saves minutes; moving the casualty or blocking the lobby slows care."),
("A guard finds an unattended bag in a metro station entrance. What should the guard do first?",
 "Ask nearby people about it", ["Open it to check inside", "Carry it to the guard room", "Push it to one side with a foot"],
 "Most unattended bags are simply forgotten. The guard first asks around; if no owner appears and it is suspicious, the area is cleared and police called. Never touch or move it."),
("An unattended item has wires showing and no owner. What should the guard do?",
 "Clear people well away", ["Stand next to it to guard it", "Cover it with a jacket", "Move it outside the building"],
 "A suspicious item is not touched or moved. People are moved well away, out of sight of it and behind solid cover, and police take over."),
("Why should a guard not use a radio or mobile phone right next to a suspected device?",
 "It might set it off", ["It wastes the battery", "Calls are recorded", "It blocks the CCTV feed"],
 "Some devices can be set off by radio signals. Guards move away to a safe distance before transmitting."),
("A caller says there is a bomb in the building. What should the guard who takes the call do?",
 "Keep them talking and take notes", ["Hang up at once and wait", "Laugh it off as a prank", "Transfer to the client's voicemail"],
 "Details such as the location, time, the caller's voice and background noises help police. A checklist by the phone helps the guard record them."),
("During a phoned bomb threat, which detail is most useful to write down?",
 "Where the caller says it is", ["The guard's own shift hours", "The weather outside the site", "How polite the caller was"],
 "The stated location and time help the police decide where to search and whether to evacuate. Background noise, accent and exact words are also noted."),
("The fire alarm sounds in an office tower. What should a guard tell occupants about the lifts?",
 "Use the stairs", ["Use the lifts quickly", "Wait in the lift lobby", "Use only the service lift"],
 "Lifts can stop or open onto a fire floor. Evacuation is by stairs unless fire-fighting or evacuation lifts are run by trained staff."),
("Where should occupants go after evacuating a building?",
 "The assembly point", ["Their cars to leave", "The nearest café", "The basement car park"],
 "At the assembly point people are counted, so the fire wardens and Civil Defence know if anyone is missing."),
("During an evacuation, a guard's role at the exit is mainly to:",
 "Keep people moving out", ["Check everyone's ID", "Collect everyone's bags", "Lock the doors behind them"],
 "Guards keep exits clear and flowing and stop people re-entering. Slowing people to check ID would cost lives."),
("A guest wants to go back inside a burning hotel for a passport. The guard should:",
 "Stop them going back in", ["Let them go quickly", "Go in for the passport", "Give them a fire extinguisher"],
 "Nobody re-enters until Civil Defence says it is safe. Belongings are replaceable; lives are not."),
("A person in a wheelchair is on the 12th floor when the alarm sounds. What should the guard do?",
 "Follow their evacuation plan", ["Leave them, as lifts are off", "Carry them down alone", "Tell them to wait for the all-clear"],
 "Sites plan for people needing help (a personal plan, refuge areas, trained staff). The guard follows it and tells Civil Defence where the person is."),
("A crowd at a concert surges toward a closed gate. What should the guard do first?",
 "Alert control to open exits", ["Hold the gate firmly shut", "Push back against the crowd", "Leave the area for safety"],
 "Crowd pressure can crush people. The guard alerts control so the plan is put in action, such as opening more exits and stopping new entries."),
("A child is reported lost in a mall. What should the guard do?",
 "Describe the child to control", ["Wait 24 hours before acting", "Drive to search the child's home", "Tell the parent to look alone"],
 "The first minutes matter. A description goes out to all staff, exits are watched and the police are informed under the site's procedure."),
("A guard smells gas in a residential building's basement. What should the guard avoid?",
 "Using light switches", ["Opening doors for air", "Moving people away", "Calling 997 from outside"],
 "Switches can spark and ignite gas. The guard leaves things as they are, moves people out and calls Civil Defence from a safe place."),
("During heavy rain in Dubai, the underground car park of a tower starts to flood. The guard should:",
 "Stop cars entering and report", ["Drive the cars out for owners", "Open the basement doors wider", "Ignore it until morning"],
 "Water rises quickly. Stopping entry, moving people to safety and reporting to management and, if needed, Civil Defence, protects life."),
("The power fails at night in a shopping centre. What should the guard do first?",
 "Check people are safe", ["Leave to find a generator", "Open all shop doors", "Switch off the fire alarm"],
 "People may be trapped in lifts or in the dark. The guard checks for them, reports the fault and watches for opportunist theft."),
("People are trapped in a stuck lift. What should the guard do?",
 "Reassure them and call for help", ["Force the lift doors open by hand", "Climb on top of the car", "Tell them to jump down"],
 "Untrained rescue causes falls. The guard keeps talking to them, calls the lift company or Civil Defence and checks they are well."),
("Which sign of hostile reconnaissance should a guard report?",
 "Someone timing guard patrols", ["A tourist asking for directions", "A shopper with many bags", "A family taking selfies"],
 "Offenders and terrorists watch sites before acting, often timing patrols or filming security. Such behaviour is noted and reported."),
("A guard is told an armed attacker is in the building. What is the guard's first priority?",
 "Help people escape or hide", ["Confront the attacker directly", "Collect the CCTV discs", "Lock the main entrance"],
 "The common advice is to escape if possible, hide if not, and tell the police on 999. Unarmed guards do not confront armed attackers."),
("After an emergency, why is the site debrief useful?",
 "It improves the plan", ["It assigns personal blame", "It replaces the police report", "It cancels all reports"],
 "A debrief records what worked and what failed, so procedures and training improve before the next incident."),
("A vehicle is parked in a fire lane outside a hotel entrance. What should the guard do?",
 "Have it moved and report it", ["Let the air out of the tyres", "Leave it for the driver", "Block it in with a barrier"],
 "Fire lanes must stay clear for Civil Defence vehicles. The guard asks for the car to be moved and reports repeated cases."),
("During a sandstorm, visibility near a site gate becomes very low. The guard should:",
 "Guide traffic slowly", ["Open all gates fully", "Leave the gate to find cover", "Wave vehicles through fast"],
 "In low visibility, vehicles and pedestrians are hard to see. The guard controls traffic at a safe pace and reports hazards."),
("An emergency plan lists 'invacuation'. This means:",
 "Moving people further inside", ["Leaving the building fast", "Searching everyone's bags", "Opening the roof doors for air"],
 "When the danger is outside (for example an attack or a gas cloud), moving people deeper into the building may be safer than evacuating."),
("A guard receives a letter that leaks a white powder. What should the guard do?",
 "Put it down and leave", ["Blow the powder away", "Shake the envelope out", "Carry it to the manager"],
 "Leave it, keep others away, close the room if possible, wash hands and call the police. Moving or shaking it spreads the substance."),
("Why do Dubai event security plans include warning and guidance signs?",
 "To direct people safely", ["To advertise the sponsors", "To mark VIP seats", "To replace guards"],
 "The 2026 bylaw (Art. 25) requires warning and guidance signs at public events as SIRA approves, alongside guarding by a licensed provider."),
("A person collapses in a crowded exhibition hall. What is the guard's first step?",
 "Check the scene is safe", ["Move the person outside", "Give them water at once", "Clear their pockets for ID"],
 "Making the area safe for the person and the guard comes first. Then check for a response, call 998 and give first aid."),
("Fire wardens and guards meet at the assembly point after an evacuation. What should they report to Civil Defence?",
 "Who is missing and where", ["Who left their desks messy", "How long the alarm rang", "Which tenants owe rent"],
 "Firefighters need to know who might still be inside and where, so they can search the right areas first."),
]
